From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <jschwender@posteo.net>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 02:37:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ohos: add a chrome-less mode to the servoshell app

`--chrome=none` drops the toolbar and the tab bar so the XComponent fills
the window. Measurement runs want the web content alone: the chrome costs
ArkUI layout on every frame and, more importantly, shrinks the viewport,
which changes how much the page has to lay out.

EntryAbility consumes the flag and does not forward it to servoshell,
whose argument parser exits the process on an option it does not
recognise. The ArkWeb test app spells it the same way, so one launch
argument now serves both.

`aa start --psn=<key>` creates a want parameter whose *name* is the whole
string after the `=` and whose value is null, so `--psn=--chrome=none`
arrives as the key `--chrome=none`. Keys are therefore split on their
first `=` before the flag is matched; what is pushed into servoshell's
argument list is still the untouched key and value, so no other launch
argument changes shape.

Validation: on a PLR-AL00, `aa start -b org.servo.servo -a EntryAbility -U <url> --psn=--chrome=none` renders m.huaweimossel.com with no toolbar and no tab bar (screenshot compared against the same launch without the flag), and a launch carrying `--psn=--tracing-filter=info,[{servo_profiling=true}]=trace` alongside it still reaches servoshell intact (630 `handle_reflow` spans in an 18 s hitrace).
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <jschwender@posteo.net>
